in reference to previous posts about "top 10 stack wands" [nh3.0]:

if the top 10 items in a stack were the only ones affected by a spell then
you'd have the ability to affect between 30 and 60 items per spell depending
on the extent of the spell. this forces you to prioritize your items which
in my opinion requires some planning and insight. the present scheme allows
you to affect several hundred (at least more than 200) items with a single
spell which seems like overkill. in my recent win i was able to exploit this
[okay, okay] but i noticed two things about it: (1) it seemed to easy and
lessened the thrill of victory and (2) it would have been just as possible
if the top ten rule were in effect but not as obvious. i think working harder
for this result would have sweetened the taste of victory. perhaps not ...

surely you jest about not winning [nh3.0] without this feature! given the
right circumstances (which i think are probable) you can win without
"stacking" at all but there's no reward for this sooo ...

why does the PEACEFUL [invisible] Demogorgon (or Juiblex or Dispater) lean
on me? They shouldn't be peaceful and act this way. This made me sick ...

